Test Case: disk_os_storage_account_type_with_restricted_location
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value

  on azapi.tf line 51, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  51:       type         = identity.value.type
     ├────────────────
     │ identity.value is null

This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: The dynamic identity block uses can() to check if identity exists, but can() returns true even when the value is null. This causes the for_each to iterate over [null], leading to an error when accessing identity.value.type.
- Fix Method: Changed from can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) to module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null for proper null checking.
- Changes Made: Modified line 49 in azapi.tf from:
    for_each = can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity) ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
  to:
    for_each = module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null ? [module.replicator.azapi_header.identity] : []
- Result: Success - Plan now runs successfully and shows acceptable drifts:
  * AzAPI resource-level attributes (ignore_null_property, locks, etc.)
  * Removed Azure API computed defaults in body
  All drifts match acceptable_drift_patterns.md

Final Result: Fix successful
